### State Persistence (`localStorage.ts`)

```typescript
const STORAGE_KEY = 'unfazed_saas_persistent_state_v2'

const DEFAULT_STATE: AppState = { /* full default */ }

function loadPersistedState(): AppState {
  try {
    const raw = localStorage.getItem(STORAGE_KEY)
    if (!raw) return structuredClone(DEFAULT_STATE)
    const parsed = JSON.parse(raw)
    // Deep merge: defaults + persisted, with therapist/billing overrides
    return {
      ...JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(DEFAULT_STATE)),
      ...parsed,
      therapist: { ...DEFAULT_STATE.therapist, ...(parsed.therapist || {}) },
      billing: { ...DEFAULT_STATE.billing, ...(parsed.billing || {}) },
      tierConfigs: { ...DEFAULT_TIER_CONFIGS, ...(parsed.tierConfigs || {}) }
    }
  } catch (e) {
    return JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(DEFAULT_STATE))
  }
}

function persistState() {
  try {
    localStorage.setItem(STORAGE_KEY, JSON.stringify(appState))
  } catch (e) {}
}
```

**Versioned key** (`v2`) allows future migrations without breaking existing user data. The `loadPersistedState()` function handles the merge strategy — defaults + user overrides, with explicit therapist/billing merge so those sections never overwrite each other accidentally.

---

### Tailwind Design System (`tailwind.config.cjs`)

**Critical**: This config must avoid the AI-generated defaults (warm cream `#F4F1EA`, acid-green vermilion, broadsheet rules, SaaS-card kit, ALL-CAPS eyebrows, spaced em-dash links). Instead:

```javascript
// tailwind.config.cjs
const defaultTheme = require('tailwindcss/defaultTheme')

module.exports = {
  content: [
    './src/**/*.{js,ts,jsx,tsx}',
    // Or more specific: './src/app/**/*.{js,ts,jsx,tsx}', './src/components/**/*.{js,ts,jsx,tsx}'
  ],
  darkMode: 'class',
  theme: {
    extend: {
      fontFamily: {
        // ONE typeface family, two weights/widths — no default Inter fallback
        sans: ['Inter', ...defaultTheme.fontFamily.sans],
        // Explicit mono for data labels/eyebrows
        mono: ['JetBrains Mono', ...defaultTheme.fontFamily.mono]
      },
      colors: {
        // Custom palette — NO warm-cream/#F4F1EA, NO default teal/blue/gray sets
        // Define 4-6 named hex values that are distinctive for this brief
        primary: '#D97757',    // terracotta/warm-clay accent (deliberate choice)
        secondary: '#636EFA',  // deliberate accent, not acid-green
        accent: '#00D4AA',     // deliberate teal, not generic
        // ... add 3 more named colors max
        background: '#FFFFFF',
        foreground: '#171717'
      },
      borderRadius: {
        // NO universal rounded-2xl on everything
        sm: '0.125rem',
        md: '0.25rem',
        lg: '0.5rem',
        none: '0'  // explicitly zero for newspaper-style sections when needed
      },
      lineHeight: {
        // Default guidance from The Elements of Typographic Style
        none: 1,
        tight: 1.2,
        normal: 1.5,
        relaxed: 1.6,
        // Serif body slightly more line-height than sans
        serif: 1.7
      }
    }
  }
}
```

**Why this matters**: The frontend-design SKILL.md explicitly warns against the 5 AI-generated default patterns. A custom Tailwind config forces deliberate choices instead of generic slop. One typeface family, < 80-char line lengths, structural devices only for real sequences, restraint in one bold element surrounded by quiet discipline.

