### View Architecture

#### 1. Landing Page (`LandingPage.tsx`)
- Hero with "Unfazed is for Clinical Practitioners" tagline + "Evaluating what works at therapy's frontier"
- Golden mountain banner SVG with trajectory vectors + floating benchmark cards
- Architecture pillars (Scheduling, Privacy, Billing) as KPI cards
- Subscription tier grid (3 columns: STARTER/PRO/CLINIC)
- **Skills needed**: `tailwind design system accessibility`, `react typescript component architecture`

#### 2. Public Booking Page (`PublicBookingPage.tsx`)
- Branded hero card ( therapist photo, badge, name, title, bio, specs)
- Service selector (individual/focused/couples)
- Date picker + IST time slot grid (atomic slot locking)
- Package bundle redeem (3/6/12 sessions)
- **Skills needed**: `healthcare web accessibility`, `razorpay payment integration saas`, `websockets realtime chat application` (for real-time slot availability)

#### 3. Therapist Dashboard (`TherapistDashboard.tsx`)
- 8 tabs navigable via vertical sidebar:
  - **A. Overview & Analytics** — 4 KPI cards, monthly revenue trend, service cohort analytics, appointment status table
  - **B. Profile & Services Editor** — branded info editor, consultation services manager (add/edit/price)
  - **C. Subscription & Plan Admin** — tier switcher, custom tier configurator (name, price, client cap, templates, packages), billing/GST editor
  - **D. Clients CRM** — add new client, search/filter client directory
  - **E. Schedule & Slots** — default duration, buffer time, blocked date overrides
  - **F. Clinical Notes (SOAP/DAP)** — template applier (SOAP/DAP/Freeform, gated by canAdvancedAnalytics), rich text editor, saved notes list, privacy enforcement (private notes never leaked to client portal)
  - **G. Payments & Packages** — payment ledger, downloadable invoices with GSTIN, package bundle creator
  - **H. Real-Time Care Chat** — encrypted channel, message sync with client portal, socket connection state
- **Skills needed**: `react state management patterns`, `testing strategies jest`, `typescript typings clinical notes`

#### 4. Client Portal (`ClientPortalPage.tsx`)
- Top banner (client name, active package balance pill, assigned therapist link, +Book New Session)
- 2-column layout:
  - **Left**: My appointments list, shared-only session notes (zero-leak privacy filter), intake form + digital consent
  - **Right**: Direct care chat with therapist, message sync
- **Skills needed**: `healthcare web accessibility`, `react testing patterns`

---

### Key Non-Functional Guarantees (Architecture Enforces These)

| Guarantee | How It's Enforced |
|---|---|
| **No AI-sloppy defaults** | Custom Tailwind config (one typeface, 4-6 named colors, <80-char line heights), explicit entitlement gates, design-plan-brief-review-build-critique loop |
| **Privacy boundary** | Notes marked `private`/`shared` at serialization; client portal query filters out `private` notes; DAP template gated behind `canAccess('NOTE_TEMPLATE', {template})`; "Strictly private — never visible in client portal" text in note content |
| **Tier consistency** | Single `canAccess()` function; every UI branch checks it; tier configs live in one `tierConfigs` object; `persistState()` serializes the whole state |
| **LocalStorage resilience** | `loadPersistedState()` with versioned key, migration helper, deep merge strategy; `persistState()` called after every mutation; fallback to DEFAULT_STATE on corruption |
| **Accessibility** | Tailwind `reduced-motion` media query, ARIA labels on forms, keyboard navigation through all interactive elements, color contrast checked against custom palette, screen-reader-friendly consent/intake forms |
| **Testability** | `canAccess()` is pure (no side effects, takes featureKey + context, returns `{allowed, reason, current, limit}`); unit tests for entitlement logic; integration tests for view switching; localStorage sync tests; snapshot tests for UI components |
| **Performance** | `react.memo` on KPI cards, `useMemo` on filtered lists, slot grid recomputation only on date/service change, debounced resize handlers, lazy-loaded route components (dynamic import for therapist tabs) |

